<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles the Simple</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/879">879</a>–<a href="/years/929">929</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Charles III of France</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles the Simple was a Carolingian King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-francia">West Francia</a>, crowned in 893 and sole king from 898. In 911, by the treaty of Saint-Clair-sur-Epte, he granted the lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rouen">Rouen</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rollo">Rollo</a>, the origin of the Duchy of Normandy. He also gained Lotharingia. Rebel nobles deposed him in 922, and he died a prisoner.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-the-simple.jpg" alt="Charles the Simple" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: cgb.fr · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Denier_sous_Charles_III_le_Simple.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
